---
// Hub for the comparison pages (entries in src/data/niches.ts whose breadcrumb starts at Compare) and comparison posts.
import Hub from '../components/hub/Hub.astro';
import { niches } from '../data/niches';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const work = new Map((await getCollection('work')).map((e) => [e.id, e.data]));
const items = niches.filter((n) => n.crumb[0]?.href === '/compare').map((n) => ({ href: `/${n.slug}`, title: n.h1, text: n.lede, image: n.hero.image ?? work.get(n.hero.work)?.preview }));
const extra = [
  { href: '/blog/design-agency-vs-freelancer-vs-in-house', title: 'Design agency vs freelancer vs in-house', text: 'The three-way choice, and what each one costs you in time.' },
  { href: '/blog/framer-vs-webflow-saas-landing-page', title: 'Framer vs Webflow for a SaaS website', text: 'How to pick, from building in both.' },
];
const guide = [
  'Most founders hire design in one of four ways: a freelancer, an agency or studio on a fixed project, a design subscription with a monthly fee, or a designer on the team. None of them is right for every stage. The choice comes down to three questions: how much design work you have every week, how soon it has to ship, and how many different skills it needs.',
  'A freelancer is the cheapest per hour and works well for a clear, single task, like one landing page or a set of ads. A studio on a fixed project costs more per hour but brings strategy, design and build in one team, with a price and a deadline agreed up front. That suits a launch, a redesign or anything with a date attached.',
  'A design subscription suits a steady stream of smaller requests, one at a time, usually turned around in about a day, with the option to pause. An in-house designer pays off once design fills most of every week and depends on knowing your product and data day to day. Hiring one usually takes weeks to months.',
  'Many startups use more than one, in order: a project with a studio to launch or redesign, a subscription while they ship weekly, and a first in-house designer once the work never stops. The pages above compare each pair side by side, with real prices and timelines.',
];
---
<Hub title="Compare your options" seoTitle="Agency vs subscription vs in-house design | Fackt" description="Honest comparisons for founders hiring design: agency vs subscription, in-house designer vs agency, freelancer, and Framer vs Webflow." eyebrow="Compare" lede="Before you hire anyone for design, here is how the options really compare, from a studio that has been on every side of it." items={items} extraTitle="More comparisons" extra={extra} guideTitle="How to choose who designs your product" guide={guide} />
